    "body": "## Motivation\n\nFixes #45953.\n\n`Glm47MoeDetector.detect_and_parse` (the non-streaming path) did not strip the captured function name, while the streaming path (`_extract_match_groups`) does. When a GLM-4.7/GLM-5 model writes a newline after the function name, `func_name` kept the trailing `\"\\n\"`, `parse_base_json` rejected the call as an undefined tool, and because the whole tool-call span had already been consumed, the response ended with **no `tool_calls` and empty `content`**.\n\nImpact (from the issue): with `tool_choice: \"required\"` on GLM-5.3 with `--tool-call-parser glm47`, about 1 in 4 forced calls was silently dropped in the reporter's tests (7/30 and 10/30); streaming the same requests gave 39/40 tool calls. Streaming and non-streaming disagreed on the same output.\n\n## Modifications\n\nOne line: strip the captured name in `detect_and_parse`, matching the streaming path's `match.group(1).strip()`:\n\n```python\nfunc_name = func_detail.group(1).strip() if func_detail.group(1) else \"\"\n```\n\n## Accuracy / Regression Tests\n\n`test/registered/unit/function_call/test_glm47_schema_types.py`:\n\n- `check_arguments` now takes the function name (the call text is built from `Glm47MoeDetector.bot_token`/`eot_token` instead of hardcoded tokens) and keeps running every case through both the non-streaming path and streaming at several chunk sizes.\n- New `test_function_name_followed_by_newline` runs a name with a trailing newline through both paths — before the fix the non-streaming branch of that case returned no calls; after it, both paths return `{\"value\": \"Paris\"}`.\n\nVerified locally before the fix: `detect_and_parse` on the issue's exact input returned `calls == []` and `normal_text == \"\"` while streaming returned `get_weather {\"city\": \"Paris\"}`; after the fix both return the call.\n\n## Test Results\n\n- `test/registered/unit/function_call/` full sweep: **610 passed, 18 failed — all 18 pre-existing on a clean tree** (verified by stashing the change and re-running; identical failure list).\n- The glm47 suite itself: 12/12 passed.\n- `ruff check --select=F401,F821,F823,UP037` (project pre-commit rules), `ruff format`, `isort`: clean.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] I have referenced the issue fixed (#45953).\n- [x] I have created at least one test case for the fix.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #41790198179](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41790198179)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41790198085](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41790198085)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #41790198072](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41790198072)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Base CI only covers the core cases, and its workload may not exercise your change. Use `/rerun-test` to run the tests your change touches, or copy this prompt for an agent:\n>\n> ```text\n> Find the registered tests this PR affects and run them with /rerun-test, following https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.agents/skills/rerun-test/SKILL.md\n> ```\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
